OrionLayer open fix 125 — MSG_CANCEL_FIELD holds the real mouse off
===================================================================

Work order 437 (parity audit of 25 November 2026, finding g of the engine notes).
orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.1), after open fix 124. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp.

MSG_INJECT_CLICK and MSG_INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK set g_injected_mouse_pending before
they push their events, so that Sync_Mouse_State_From_SDL stands aside until the
queue is pumped (open fix 3). MSG_CANCEL_FIELD pushes the same pair of events
(a right click on the field's centre) and did not: the physical mouse could
rewrite the release through the coalescing in Enqueue_Mouse_Input_Event, which
is the defect open fix 3 describes.

The change. One line, g_injected_mouse_pending = true, before the events are
pushed, with the same reason beside it. The flag is cleared by the next pump
as for the other two commands.

Proved: ext_api.cpp syntax-checked on the scratch clone with the build's flags;
the branch built. Live: UNVERIFIED, see doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 125.

